      "type": "paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Air Air where Pri is the primary signal, T is the total measured signal, CS is the estimated cross-scatter, and Air is the reference air signal. To reduce noise amplification, T is smoothed before subtraction. Detailed implementation of the cross-scatter correction algorithm is provided in Supplementary Information S2.\n\nEvaluation of cross-scatter correction performance The performance of the proposed cross-scatter correction method was evaluated through three assessments: qualitative comparison with an established correction approach, and quantitative comparisons of spatial resolution and low-contrast detectability with vs without correction. For the qualitative comparison, representative CT images were reconstructed using the proposed method and a method based on the model-based correction described by Petersilka et al [17], hereinafter referred to as the “reference method”, respectively. The resulting images",
